{"ts":"2026-09-07T13:41:04.384Z","event":"attempt","ticket":"T-26-08","pr":35,"n":1,"role":"review-fix","model":"sonnet","outcome":"pushed","signature":"none","head":"ddace856675729e74ca03c050f5ef6fdb5869c71","hypothesis":"Both Copilot findings were real: the Source of truth line never carried repo identity so the legacy-match check it described couldn't run, and 'repo slug' was introduced but never used by the label templates which took <owner>/<repo> separately. Rewrote the pointer template to carry <owner>/<repo> (written into legacy issues at migration time so a later run from a different repo sees the claim), and dropped the slug term in favor of <owner>/<repo> throughout."}
